{
  "manufacturer": "Contemporary Controls",
  "manufacturer_slug": "contemporary-controls",
  "model": "Kohler MPAC 1500 transfer switch controller via BASgatewayLX",
  "short_model": "BASgatewayLX Kohler MPAC 1500",
  "model_slug": "basgatewaylx-kohler-mpac-1500",
  "aliases": [
    "MPAC 1500",
    "Kohler ATS",
    "MPAC1500"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Automatic transfer switch controller",
  "applies_to": "Kohler transfer switches with the MPAC 1500 controller on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Kohler MPAC 1500: 135 objects (47 AI, 88 AO), 79 polled by default. Inputs give the system overview word, normal and emergency source line-neutral and line-line voltages, frequencies, load currents, transition data, mode and switch position, and the active time delay. Outputs hold the nominal ratings, time delays and pickup/dropout settings, plus unpolled programmable I/O.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Kohler_MPAC_1500_ATS_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the MPAC 1500 Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/tp6113.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 79 of the 135 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Kohler_MPAC_1500_ATS_a",
    "doc_number": "Kohler_MPAC_1500_ATS_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Kohler_MPAC_1500_ATS_a_LX.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Read the system overview word, source voltages and frequencies and the mode/switch position register. Most outputs are settings, not commands.",
